nd dimitresque  with a more vampire-esque one but just  reading into that and seeing the  build-up and the puzzle piece of reading  the item descriptions when lore come  together  really elevated the material and i just  love seeing that in a resident evil game  on top of that we got to find out a  little bit more about elements i don't  want to spoil in case you haven't played  the game because you really should but  elements about the lore that really  helped explain some of the absolute  weirdness and things that happened in  resident evil 7 and the beginning of  village that have you scratching your  head and now all that is explained and  tied up in a nice little bow so i really  appreciate about that about village all  of that together is why resident evil  village just stands out again as another  fantastic entry in the resident evil  franchise what resident evil village did  was take elements of all of the previous  games and then merge them together for a  totally unique experience and way to  play resident evil there's a reason that  this franchise has continued to stand  the test of time and be one of the names  if not the name  in horror in video games and resident  evil village just continues that and  that is why it is one of the best games  of the year and you should definitely  check it out if you haven't  go do it  this is where it all began  nowhere  this is where it all  ended  dad what are you doing here well we're  here to support you son  will we  we all make mistakes  why are you taking so  long  [Music]  i'm getting less sure i want to see this  oh no  i don't think you want to see this at  all  psychonauts 2 is a really deceiving game  on the surface it's this over-the-top  colorful funny ambitious 3d platformer  but the moment you start to peel back  the layers you reveal a game that's  really about second chances and  forgiveness and maybe above all else  it's about  at being empathetic and understanding to  the people around you  and those very concepts are seeded  through nearly every single aspect of  the game from the mechanics to the  character's motivations to the very  worlds you explore every single angle  and part of the scheme was meticulously  detailed to service its themes its  themes of mental health its themes of  acceptance psychonauts 2 takes all these  incredibly heavy concepts and packages  them in such a way that is so effortless  and approachable that it even takes you  a moment to really digest exactly what  it is that's going on in that game every  single level is the mind of a person  that you explore and each single person  like you and me battle with their own  problems whether that's ptsd anxiety  imposter syndrome it's all there but the  thing that makes psychonauts 2 so  brilliant and how it approaches these  rather sensitive topics is when you go  into these people's minds instead of  trying to solve their problems instead  of that kind of being the end goal  instead you walk away  understanding that person and where they  came from and better having an  empathetic idea of why they are the way  they are but even more importantly that  is what defines them into the wonderful  character  that they've become even the idea of  something like regrets and doubts and  panic attacks are the basis for the very  enemies that you fight in that game and  because it's done in such a colorful  fun humorous way that's never quite  spoon feeding it to you you can play  this game and just have a good time for  what it is but it's all the more  rewarding to actually take a step back  and take a look at the world and see how  every single concept just works in  complete tandem with each other it is  so  impressive even though psychonauts 2 is  the sequel to a 16 year old game it did  more than just exceed my expectations as  a fan of the original but instead stand  on its own two feet as a classic in its  own right and is more than well  deserving to be among the best games of  this year  o